### 8e.5-A. Path A Eligibility Gate

Check ALL four criteria. Any failure → mark eligibility **ineligible** and skip to 8e.5-C (the test is still committed there if it passed Step 3; the issue retains `verified (Path B)`).

**A1 — Mocked-unit only:** The test must mock all external dependencies using `vi.mock(...)` or `jest.mock(...)`. Must not use a real `DATABASE_URL`, `REDIS_URL`, or real network endpoint. Must not use `child_process`, `exec`, `spawn`, or real `fetch` to non-localhost URLs outside a mock.

**A2 — Runner allowlist:** The test runner must be Vitest or Jest (identified from the project's test command). Any other runner (pytest, mocha, tap, jasmine) → ineligible.

**A3 — Static no-sink pre-scan:** Read the test file. If it contains any of the following outside a mock block → ineligible:
- `fs.rmSync`, `fs.unlinkSync`, `fs.writeFileSync`
- `child_process`, `execSync`, `spawnSync`
- `fetch(` with a non-localhost/non-mock URL
- `process.exit(`

**A4 — Workspace symlink check:**

```bash
find node_modules -maxdepth 2 -type l 2>/dev/null | head -10
```

Read a sample of the symlink targets. If any `node_modules/@org/pkg` symlink points to `../../packages/...` (workspace-linked source), mark **ineligible** — symlinking `node_modules` into a parent worktree would drag fix-era workspace package source into the parent run, silently defeating discrimination. (This is a monorepo workspace pattern.)

If all four checks pass → **eligible**, proceed to 8e.5-B.

