### 8e.5-B. Blind Discrimination Subagent (Path A)

Dispatch a subagent with ONLY these inputs (no diff, no fix description, no source code, no commit message — structural blindness prevents maker/checker fusion):

> You are a deterministic discrimination validator. Your single job: prove whether a regression test can distinguish pre-fix (buggy) code from post-fix (fixed) code, by running it against both commit states. You are not permitted to read the fix's source diff or the bug report.
>
> **Your inputs (all you know):**
> - Test file path: `{path/to/new-test-file}`
> - FIX_SHA: `{FIX_SHA}` — the fixed commit (working tree is already at this state)
> - PARENT_SHA: `{PARENT_SHA}` — the commit before the fix
> - Test command: `{detected test command} {new-test-file} --reporter=json`
> - PKG_CWD: `{absolute path to the package.json directory for this test's package}`
>
> **Phase A — Fix-side (3 runs on current working tree at FIX_SHA):**
> From PKG_CWD, run the test command 3 times. Each run must show all tests PASS. If any run fails or produces an error → write `{"verdict": "inconclusive", "reason": "fix-side failure or flakiness"}` to `issue-NNN-testcheck.json` and stop.
>
> **Phase B — Parent-side (3 runs in isolated worktree at PARENT_SHA):**
>
> 1. Create a detached worktree at PARENT_SHA using the pattern from `lib/worktree.ts` in this repo: `git worktree add --detach .gstack-worktrees/qa-patha-NNN-<timestamp> PARENT_SHA`. Use a unique runId to avoid collisions with sibling sessions.
>
> 2. Copy ONLY the test file into the worktree (preserving its relative path): `cp <test-file-path> .gstack-worktrees/<runId>/<relative-path>`. Do NOT copy source files — the worktree already has PARENT_SHA source. Do NOT copy `node_modules`.
>
> 3. Symlink `node_modules` for dependency resolution: from the worktree root, create a symlink: `ln -s <absolute-path-to-repo-root>/node_modules .gstack-worktrees/<runId>/node_modules`. This brings in the test framework and npm deps without bringing workspace-linked source (workspace symlinks were already screened out by the eligibility gate).
>
> 4. From `{worktree-root}/{PKG_CWD relative to repo root}`, run the test command 3 times, capturing `--reporter=json` output for each run.
>
> 5. Cleanup: `git worktree remove --force .gstack-worktrees/<runId> && git worktree prune`.
>
> **Per-run classification rules (apply to each run's `--reporter=json` output):**
>
> Evaluate in this strict order — earlier conditions supersede later ones:
>
> *Step 1 — Suite-level load check (evaluate first, before per-case logic):*
> Classify the whole run as **LOAD_FAIL** if ANY of the following holds:
> - `numTotalTests === 0` (suite failed to collect; primary signal for both runners)
> - Vitest: file-level `status === "failed"` with empty `assertionResults` array AND a top-level error `message` present
> - Jest: `testResults[0].testExecError` is set (note: absent on many Jest versions even for load failures — `numTotalTests === 0` is the more reliable signal)
> If any of the above → whole run = **LOAD_FAIL**. Stop. Do not evaluate per-case logic.
>
> *Step 2 — Per-case classification (evaluate ALL cases before rolling up):*
> For each entry in `assertionResults`, classify it independently:
> - Entry is **assertion-shaped** if `failureMessages[0]` matches ANY of: `AssertionError`, `expected .* to`, `Received:`, `Expected:`, `to be`, `to equal`, `to match`, `to throw` with value context
> - Entry is **load-shaped** if `failureMessages[0]` matches ANY of: `TypeError:`, `is not a function`, `is not defined`, `ReferenceError:`, `Cannot find module`, `SyntaxError:`, `Failed to load`, `Cannot read`, `STACK_TRACE_ERROR`
> - Ambiguous (neither pattern clearly matches) → classify entry as **load-shaped** (fail-closed default)
>
> *Step 3 — Roll-up rule (LOAD-SHAPE DOMINATES — this is the critical invariant):*
> - If ANY case is load-shaped → whole run = **LOAD_FAIL**. Load-shape dominance is unconditional: the presence of an assertion-shaped case in the SAME file does NOT rescue the run to ASSERTION_FAIL.
> - If ALL failing cases are assertion-shaped AND at least one is present → whole run = **ASSERTION_FAIL**
> - If all `assertionResults` entries have `status === "passed"` → whole run = **PASS**
> - Runner exits non-zero with no parseable JSON, or run exceeds 30s → **TIMEOUT**
>
> **Discrimination verdict (applied after all 6 runs are classified):**
> - ALL 3 parent runs = ASSERTION_FAIL AND ALL 3 fix runs = PASS → verdict: `verified (deterministic)`
> - ANY parent run = PASS (test ran cleanly but didn't trigger on the bug) → verdict: `tautological`
> - ANY parent run = LOAD_FAIL or TIMEOUT → verdict: `inconclusive`
> - ANY fix run ≠ PASS → verdict: `inconclusive` (fix-side instability)
> - Mixed results across parent runs → verdict: `inconclusive`
>
> **Output ONLY this JSON** (write to `{REPORT_DIR}/screenshots/issue-NNN-testcheck.json`):
> ```json
> {
>   "verdict": "verified (deterministic)" | "tautological" | "inconclusive",
>   "fix_sha": "{FIX_SHA}",
>   "parent_sha": "{PARENT_SHA}",
>   "fix_runs": [
>     {"attempt": 1, "classification": "PASS", "summary": "all N tests passed"},
>     ...
>   ],
>   "parent_runs": [
>     {
>       "attempt": 1,
>       "classification": "ASSERTION_FAIL" | "LOAD_FAIL" | "PASS" | "TIMEOUT",
>       "summary": "brief description of what happened",
>       "failure_message_excerpt": "first 150 chars of failureMessages[0] for each failing case (include per-case classification label)",
>       "load_shape_dominated": true | false
>     },
>     ...
>   ],
>   "assertion_diff": "one-sentence description of what the test asserted that differed between parent and fix (null if verdict is not verified)"
> }
> ```
>
> **Fail-closed invariants:**
> - Never classify a LOAD_FAIL run as ASSERTION_FAIL. Load-shape from ANY case dominates.
> - Ambiguous `failureMessages` → load-shaped. Do not guess "this looks like an assertion error" without a clear matcher pattern.
> - Do NOT read the fix source diff, the commit message, or the bug report.
> - If worktree setup fails for any reason → write `{"verdict": "inconclusive", "reason": "worktree setup failed: <error>"}` and exit.

If dispatch fails or returns no parseable JSON → write `{"verdict": "inconclusive", "reason": "subagent unavailable"}`.

